xtras/9dc3ce1b1f83af6936d29257bd7d002c.mp4?t=1754354473\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Who It\u2019s For</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fans of <strong>space arcade chaos</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Players who crave <strong>reflex-driven puzzles</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gamers who secretly love science but want to earn it through action, not textbooks</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Join the Color Core</strong><br>Follow <strong>@t3ampo</strong> on Instagram, Twitch, and X to see behind-the-scenes builds, dev drops, Astropilot lore, and community shoutouts.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3755720/extras/44c5911cb702f3f4f7f4b3aa0d0b5cbd.avif?t=1754354473\" data-has-big width=800 height=450 /></span></p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Embark on an educational space odyssey in Mix It!, a captivating Astropilot training adventure. Master the physics of light through dynamic gameplay, stunning visuals, and award-winning sound design. Explore, learn, and conquer the universe in this genre-defying educational experience.",
    "supported_languages": "English, Spanish - Latin America, German, Japanese, Portuguese - Brazil, Simplified Chinese",
    "reviews": "\u201cThis game can be used to support student instruction of electromagnetic radiation. Specifically, the students will learn about light waves and colors that reflect off of surfaces. As the game stands, students will need some background information about light frequency and wave lengths in order to understand some concepts in the game. With some additional instructional pieces, this game could be a great resource!\u201d<br>Legends of Learning<br><br>\u201cStudents will enjoy playing this game which helps them understand how light and color are related. The game contains three levels, each of which present the information and then take the player to a simulation where they interact with the concept, dodging asteroids or repelling other enemy ships. Kids will like the video-game quality, making this a good choice to add to your playlist.\u201d<br>Legends of Learning<br>",
